// expect-error: String.ljust() takes between 1 and 2 arguments but 0 were given
// p115 — wrong argument count to a method is reported (v7.8.0).
// Calls to built-in methods weren't arity-checked: a missing argument
// reached codegen and died as "malformed IR". (Since v7.9.1 `pad` has a
// default, so `ljust(4)` is fine and `ljust()` is the error case.)
define main() -> void {
    print("ab".ljust())
}
